Subject: [PATCH] input-method: resend the keymap when a keyboard replaces it

Against Hyprland v0.57.0 (src/protocols/InputMethodV2.{cpp,hpp}).

The keyboard grab sends a keymap only when the keyboard changes. An
on-screen keyboard (squeekboard, through virtual-keyboard-v1) replaces its
keymap while it stays the same keyboard, for example on a layout change,
so an input method holding the grab (fcitx5) kept decoding its keycodes
with the old keymap: squeekboard's space reached fcitx5 as "l". Letters
happened to keep their codes.

Compare the keymap too, and resend it when it changed.

--- i/src/protocols/InputMethodV2.cpp
+++ w/src/protocols/InputMethodV2.cpp
@@ -29,10 +29,14 @@
 
 void CInputMethodKeyboardGrabV2::sendKeyboardData(SP<IKeyboard> keyboard) {
 
-    if (keyboard == m_lastKeyboard)
+    // A virtual keyboard (an on-screen keyboard) replaces its keymap while it
+    // stays the same keyboard, so compare the keymap too, or the input method
+    // keeps decoding its keycodes with the old one.
+    if (keyboard == m_lastKeyboard && keyboard->m_xkbKeymapV1String == m_lastKeymap)
         return;
 
     m_lastKeyboard = keyboard;
+    m_lastKeymap   = keyboard->m_xkbKeymapV1String;
 
     auto keymapFD = allocateSHMFile(keyboard->m_xkbKeymapV1String.length() + 1);
     if UNLIKELY (!keymapFD.isValid()) {
--- i/src/protocols/InputMethodV2.hpp
+++ w/src/protocols/InputMethodV2.hpp
@@ -98,6 +98,7 @@
     WP<CInputMethodV2>                m_owner;
 
     WP<IKeyboard>                     m_lastKeyboard;
+    std::string                       m_lastKeymap;
 };
 
 class CInputMethodPopupV2 {
